    "number": 271,
    "title": "chore: pin GitHub Actions used by lint.yml to specific commit SHAs",
    "body": "Closes #85\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\nThis PR updates the GitHub Actions in our CI workflows and user-facing templates to be pinned to specific commit SHAs rather than mutable tags (`@master`, `@v1`, and `@v4`). Pinning to exact SHAs improves security by ensuring we always run immutable, reviewed code and protects against upstream compromises or breaking changes.\r\n\r\n### What Changed\r\n- Pinned `actions/checkout` to `11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262` (`# v4`) across all workflows.\r\n- Pinned `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` to `e97e2d8cc328f1b50210efc529dca0028893a2d9` (`# v1`) across all workflows.\r\n- Synchronized these changes across `.github/workflows/lint.yml`, `docs/integration.md`, and `templates/github-action.yml`.\r\n\r\n*(Note: Prior to this PR, `.github/workflows/lint.yml` was already tracking `@v1` for `rust-toolchain` instead of `@master` as originally reported, but the mutable tag issue still applied and is now resolved via the SHA pin.)*\r\n\r\n### Acceptance Criteria Checklist\r\n- [x] `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` in `.github/workflows/lint.yml` is pinned to a specific released tag or commit SHA rather than `@master`.\r\n- [x] `actions/checkout` is pinned consistently across the workflow.\r\n- [x] `templates/github-action.yml` and the copy of the workflow embedded in `docs/integration.md` receive the same treatment.\r\n- [x] CI passes on the pinned versions.\r\n- [x] Any pin expressed as a raw SHA carries a trailing comment naming the human-readable version.\r\n\r\n### Security Note\r\nThe workflow definitions now securely reference immutable SHAs for third-party actions, preventing arbitrary code execution risks from mutating tags.",
